\1\n    <div id="site-header"></div>
    <!-- Header -->
    
    <main class="lesson-container py-4">
        <!-- Breadcrumb -->
        <div id="tutorial-header"></div>
        
        <div class="content lesson-content" style="font-size: 1.05rem; line-height: 1.7; color: var(--text-secondary);">

            <p>Theory is important, but practical application solves problems. These generic fictional case studies demonstrate structured isolation.</p>
            
            <h3>Case 1: "The Internet is Slow for Everyone"</h3>
            <p><strong>Symptom:</strong> Multiple users across different floors report slow internet.</p>
            <p><strong>What to Check First:</strong> Scope and <a href="network-monitoring-fundamentals.html">monitoring</a> dashboards. Is WAN utilization at 100%? Are there interface errors on the core switch?</p>
            <p><strong>Tools:</strong> SNMP graphs, firewall traffic logs, <code>ping</code> to external IPs to check for <a href="packet-loss-troubleshooting.html">packet loss</a> or <a href="network-latency-troubleshooting.html">latency</a>.</p>
            <p><strong>Findings & Root Cause Example:</strong> Monitoring shows the 1 Gbps WAN link is maxed out. NetFlow analysis reveals a single server is downloading a massive unthrottled backup from the cloud.</p>
            <p><strong>Resolution:</strong> Apply <a href="qos-explained.html">QoS</a> traffic shaping to the backup process to prevent it from starving business traffic.</p>
            
            <h3>Case 2: "One VLAN Cannot Access the Internet"</h3>
            <p><strong>Symptom:</strong> The Sales VLAN works, but the HR VLAN has no Internet access.</p>
            <p><strong>What to Check First:</strong> Client IP addressing. Do they have a valid IP or a 169.254.x.x address? Can they ping their default gateway?</p>
            <p><strong>Tools:</strong> <code>ipconfig /all</code>, <code>ping</code>.</p>
            <p><strong>Findings & Root Cause Example:</strong> Clients have correct IPs and can ping the firewall (their gateway). However, traffic dies there. Inspection of the <a href="stateful-firewall-explained.html">Stateful Firewall</a> shows no NAT rule translates the new HR subnet to the public IP.</p>
            <p><strong>Resolution:</strong> Add the HR subnet to the outbound NAT policy.</p>
            
            <h3>Case 3: "Website Works by IP but Not Hostname"</h3>
            <p><strong>Symptom:</strong> Users can reach a partner portal via <code>http://203.0.113.50</code>, but typing <code>http://portal.example.com</code> fails immediately.</p>
            <p><strong>What to Check First:</strong> Name resolution. Is the client using the correct DNS server?</p>
            <p><strong>Tools:</strong> <code>nslookup portal.example.com</code> or <code>Resolve-DnsName</code>.</p>
            <p><strong>Findings & Root Cause Example:</strong> The internal DNS server returns an NXDOMAIN (does not exist). A recent domain migration resulted in a stale conditional forwarder pointing to a decommissioned DNS server.</p>
            <p><strong>Resolution:</strong> Update the internal DNS server's forwarding rules.</p>
            
            <h3>Case 4: "Application is Slow but Ping is Fine"</h3>
            <p><strong>Symptom:</strong> Users complain a database application is terribly slow, but <code>ping</code> from the client to the server shows &lt;1ms latency and 0 loss.</p>
            <p><strong>What to Check First:</strong> Is it a network problem or a server problem? "Ping works" only proves ICMP routing is healthy.</p>
            <p><strong>Tools:</strong> <code>Test-NetConnection -Port</code>, Wireshark, server CPU/Disk metrics.</p>
            <p><strong>Findings & Root Cause Example:</strong> Wireshark shows the client sends a TCP request, and the network delivers it instantly. However, the server takes 4 seconds to generate the TCP response payload. Server logs indicate 100% disk I/O utilization.</p>
            <p><strong>Resolution:</strong> Escalate to the Server/Database team. The network is healthy.</p>
        
        </div>
        
